# retro-quiet-guard — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# id                | world | patch | env                                 | expect              | params
prepare-ok          |       |       | PREP_RC=0                           | prepare-ok          |
quiet-push-ok       |       |       | PREP_RC=3 CURL_RC_1=0               | quiet-push-ok       |
quiet-push-retry-ok |       |       | PREP_RC=3 CURL_RC_1=1 CURL_RC_2=0   | quiet-push-retry-ok |
quiet-push-fails    |       |       | PREP_RC=3 CURL_RC_1=1 CURL_RC_2=1   | quiet-push-fails    |
prepare-fails       |       |       | PREP_RC=1                           | prepare-fails       |
# ── the PromQL guard (homelab#3140): a named series reads its OWN gauge, not the ledger ──
# A result > 0 fires (prepare runs --no-ledger); == 0 is a quiet week (the quiet push, as above);
# an EMPTY result, a Prometheus error or a dead Prometheus FAILS the run — an absent gauge is a
# broken exporter, never a quiet week (the ledger guard's "0 tasks is a dead collector" rule).
expr-fires          |       |       | SERIES=feedback-triage GUARD_EXPR=max(g)>bool(604800) PROM_VALUE=1 PREP_RC=0      | expr-fires          |
expr-quiet          |       |       | SERIES=feedback-triage GUARD_EXPR=max(g)>bool(604800) PROM_VALUE=0 CURL_RC_1=0   | expr-quiet          |
expr-absent         |       |       | SERIES=feedback-triage GUARD_EXPR=max(g)>bool(604800) PROM_VALUE=absent          | expr-absent         |
expr-error          |       |       | SERIES=feedback-triage GUARD_EXPR=max(g)>bool(604800) PROM_VALUE=error           | expr-error          |
expr-prom-down      |       |       | SERIES=feedback-triage GUARD_EXPR=max(g)>bool(604800) PROM_VALUE=down            | expr-prom-down      |
